From: atty303 <atty303@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 02:55:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] winhttp: use 90 second response timeout default

WINHTTP_OPTION_RECEIVE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT defaults to 90 seconds on Windows.
Wine currently substitutes 21 seconds when the option was not explicitly set,
which can time out a slow response before applications expect it to.

Use the documented default without changing explicitly configured timeouts.

diff --git a/dlls/winhttp/request.c b/dlls/winhttp/request.c
--- a/dlls/winhttp/request.c
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/request.c
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(winhttp);
 
 #define DEFAULT_KEEP_ALIVE_TIMEOUT 30000
 
-#define ACTUAL_DEFAULT_RECEIVE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT 21000
+#define ACTUAL_DEFAULT_RECEIVE_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT 90000
 
 static int request_receive_response_timeout( struct request *req )
 {
